From: Gezim <gezimos@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Kompakt: a stray tap beside the PIN pad does not close it

SceneContainerStartable answers every falsing detection by switching to the lockscreen, which hides the Bouncer overlay. A tap beside the PIN keys, or a run of fast taps, pushed the falsing belief past 0.9 and closed the pad. Falsing is now ignored while the Bouncer is showing; Back and the swipe down still close it.
---
 .../systemui/scene/domain/startable/SceneContainerStartable.kt  | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/scene/domain/startable/SceneContainerStartable.kt b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/scene/domain/startable/SceneContainerStartable.kt
index ccd0302f7ddc..e6fa4d3ba384 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/scene/domain/startable/SceneContainerStartable.kt
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/scene/domain/startable/SceneContainerStartable.kt
@@ -918,6 +918,8 @@ constructor(
                     awaitClose { falsingManager.removeFalsingBeliefListener(listener) }
                 }
                 .collect {
+                    // Kompakt: a stray tap beside the PIN pad does not close it.
+                    if (Overlays.Bouncer in sceneInteractor.currentOverlays.value) return@collect
                     val loggingReason = "Falsing detected."
                     switchToScene(targetSceneKey = Scenes.Lockscreen, loggingReason = loggingReason)
                 }
